{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation","id":1268632,"title":"Map-to-globe spherical Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-18T14:11:26-08:00","id":1268632,"title":"Map-to-globe spherical Creation","content":"Rather than necro the last thread I found on this topic, I thought I'd share this <i>incredibly</i> cool website I found, and what turned out to be the near-perfect visualization for my/our image of a round Creation in the Third Age:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/ByPJDiA6X\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/ByPJDiA6X\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/ByPJDiA6X\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.maptoglobe.com/ByPJDiA6X </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Y'know that red banner on the left of the First Age map? It's perfect for the swath of Creation still held by the Wyld...if the borders are pushed back to roughly First Age levels, of course. The ice cap and fire cap (it's still a universe run by/on magic) are overrun in the Age of Sorrows, as are much of the regions around the poles of Wood and Water. I figure enough white space could do the same thing for a Second Age map on maptoglobe.com. (Great site, IMO.) This is really helpful to us, since our campaign is going to steal Shards stuff for the Outside Space portions of the campaign, and it'll let me threw maps from other game supplements onto this site for new worlds as the heroes find them.<br /> <br /> So, is anyone else going to play with this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T01:55:04-08:00","id":1268762,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'm not a fan of the gigantic wyld zone.<br /> To me the appeal of having Creation as a globe is that you connect the far west to the far east turning the 'empty' edge of the world into a major trade route and I can see a little wyld making things interesting, but this much makes the prospect of travel from Saigoth to Sperimin a &quot;turn around and go the other way&quot; deal, even to most Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:57:04-08:00","id":1268771,"title":"","content":"Anyone think of bending it the other way? As in nake it on the inside surface of a hollow sphere. Kinda like Pelucidar or a Dyson Shell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 11-19-2018, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:24:02-08:00","id":1268780,"title":"","content":"I think one issue there is that the elemental poles are all wonky. If I was designing a spherical creation I'd probably place the outer poles at the corners of a tetrahedron within the planet, with Earth at the centre. <br /> <br /> I mean sure, it takes some significance away from mount meru but it's not like it does all that much anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:06:38-08:00","id":1268801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tried it with the updated 3e map, I like this site.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:49:12-08:00","id":1268815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1268801#post1268801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm</a><br /> <br /> Tried it with the updated 3e map, I like this site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly makes a much better globe in my opinion, I like how the Dreaming Sea connects pretty seamlessly to the great Western Ocean.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T06:22:40-08:00","id":1268828,"title":"","content":"I thought the 3rd ed globe was very interesting, as it helps you compare distances to the real world (flat real-world maps are normally Mercator projections, which have misleading size).<br /> <br /> But then I realised the world isn't exactly the same size as Creation, so I thought I'd compare them.<br /> <br /> The real world is about 25000 miles around, and 12500 miles north-to-south (not exactly, of course; it's wider around the middle than north-to-south). That's north-to-south overland of course, not through the middle.<br /> <br /> Creation, according to the 3rd ed map, is about 11000 miles North-to-South, and 17000 miles East-to-West. Though of course, that's just the map... obviously the edges are quite nebulous, as they bleed into the Wyld.<br /> <br /> So, I think you can use this map to compare North-to-South distances pretty well, but East-to-West isn't quite as much as in the real world.<br /> <br /> Obviously if you know all the numbers you can compare it anyway, but I think it's easier to visualise with pictures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T14:01:51-08:00","id":1268979,"title":"","content":"The place where Wood and Water overlap would be an interesting region. Aquatic plants in profusion perhaps? I would be tempted to spread them out so that Earth, Wood, and Water are equidistant around the equator.<br /> <br /> Which on this globe would put the Pole of Water somewhere north of the Caul, and the Pole of Wood around Ixcoatli","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 11-19-2018, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:09:14-08:00","id":1269077,"title":"","content":"I honestly really dislike that first age map from 2e, because it doesn't sell the idea of creation as larger in the first age much at all. In my opinion, each axis of the map should have gotten at least 50% longer (AKA 1 quarter on each end) for the first age map. Or rather, I believe that a 1/3 reduction in the overall dimensions of creation from its first age borders is the absolute least that should have come of a series of events like the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade, after a thousand or so years of the most fragile borderlands wyld shaped in the first age being gradually eroded by a relative lack of global connectivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T21:21:46-08:00","id":1269100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1269077#post1269077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly really dislike that first age map from 2e, because it doesn't sell the idea of creation as larger in the first age much at all. In my opinion, each axis of the map should have gotten at least 50% longer (AKA 1 quarter on each end) for the first age map. Or rather, I believe that a 1/3 reduction in the overall dimensions of creation from its first age borders is the absolute least that should have come of a series of events like the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade, after a thousand or so years of the most fragile borderlands wyld shaped in the first age being gradually eroded by a relative lack of global connectivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got mixed feelings on the map's size.<br /> For DotFA as an alternate setting in the High First Age, it's horribly uninspired and makes all the talk about Creation before the Balorian Crusade seem like bluster and propaganda.<br /> For DotFA as a collection of source books, it constrains the relevant locations to places that Age of Sorrows PCs can for the most part still interact with.<br /> <br /> A more general complaint I have is how sparse it is, whatever the mindset towards the suppliment this should've been one of the most thorough maps of Creation that way people playing in this setting can look at the sheer number of cities and go &quot;yes, it feels like 10 billion people live in this version of Creation&quot; while people using DotFA as a source books could go &quot;huh there used to be 4 First Age cities in the area where my game is going on, maybe I can send my PCs to one?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T21:54:36-08:00","id":1269120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1268801#post1268801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.maptoglobe.com/SJpdEVxRm</a><br /> <br /> Tried it with the updated 3e map, I like this site.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s all fun and games until the entire East Coast is a straight line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T21:58:37-08:00","id":1269123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1269100#post1269100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whatever the mindset towards the suppliment this should've been one of the most thorough maps of Creation that way people playing in this setting can look at the sheer number of cities and go &quot;yes, it feels like 10 billion people live in this version of Creation&quot; while people using DotFA as a source books could go &quot;huh there used to be 4 First Age cities in the area where my game is going on, maybe I can send my PCs to one?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So like... a map that is just covered with lots of extra dots? Do they all need to be named?<br /> <br /> I feel as though any kind of map at that scale that isn't colour-coded with a population key isn't really effective at conveying the kind of information that you're looking for there.<br /> <br /> Although... no, there are angles I'm not considering properly there. If a sparse Creation is compared...<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is that neither version has familiar nation states, although even those are limited in the kind of information they convey... what would be different in a map of China today from one sixty years ago...<br /> <br /> It is way too late, and I have been sleeping terribly for more than a week.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T23:32:53-08:00","id":1269139,"title":"","content":"I think you make fair points about cities.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... One way to make it feel less sparse would be to expand the arable land. In some parts of the map that's been done, but the South basically looks the same; the desert with no cities (well, one) just extends further South, which actually makes the occupied coastal strip look smaller. If green land with cities extended further South, it'd be an obvious change from the Age of Sorrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T04:53:50-08:00","id":1269182,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not suggesting a random scattershot of dots to try and convey that there's 20 times as many people.<br /> <br /> The East doesn't need more cities but like the South, The North could have also benefited from a visual indicator that it was once better cultivated for a human population and with international travel and commerce much easier, the West could do more with it's smaller islands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-20-2018, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T05:08:52-08:00","id":1269185,"title":"","content":"Maybe a map that was colour coded with population density could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T05:42:48-08:00","id":1269191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1269182#post1269182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The North could have also benefited from a visual indicator that it was once better cultivated for a human population</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the landmass between the Inland Sea and the frosty parts is a lot thicker, at least.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I have a preference for a First Age in which the settlements themselves could be magically climate controlled while the surrounding territory remained much the same, since I think that overriding their elemental characteristics removes a lot of their charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">with international travel and commerce much easier</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you convey <i>that</i> on a map?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T06:39:45-08:00","id":1269205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1269191#post1269191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I have a preference for a First Age in which the settlements themselves could be magically climate controlled while the surrounding territory remained much the same, since I think that overriding their elemental characteristics removes a lot of their charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but if you don't put the settlements on the map and you don't talk about them they won't exist in most people's perceptions of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you convey <i>that</i> on a map?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda already said, but you sniped my post so I'll give an example. <br /> Wu Jian on the Ex3 map helps to establish the logistics of taking a ship from the Blessed Isle to Coral and Wavecrest and its inclusion makes the western ocean seem less desolate. I think if you don't establish what's on some of the islands people are just going to default to a mental image of natives in loincloths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T06:55:38-08:00","id":1269210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1268632-map-to-globe-spherical-creation?p=1269205#post1269205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I kinda already said, but you sniped my post so I'll give an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>{checks again}<br /> <br /> Okay, I can see what you were saying now, it's just really hard to tell how the points in that post were connected due to the severe lack of commas.<br /> <br /> Without them, it read as saying &quot;the map could show travel and commerce&quot;, rather than &quot;with travel and commerce, you could do more with the West&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T10:51:51-08:00","id":1275845,"title":"","content":"I Want to Play in this globe thing too =)<br /> I\u00b4ve saw all other projects and sorry.... I have to disagree with them.<br /> <br /> Wyld has &quot;eaten&quot; lots of parts of the planet, no one would know or dare to rediscover what proportion of Creation is covered in Wyld.<br /> <br /> Lets go to my interpretation of Creation!! The &quot;limits of the world&quot; are not straight lines in the end of the map but something like &quot; I won\u00b4t fucking dare to go near that place lines&quot; to know what that is.<br /> <br /> Next to the cardinal Points is the epicenter of the Elemental Poles: Too far in South Would be uber Hot and then pure Caos..... too far in the west would be water vortexes (or floating water) and then pure Chaos..... AND SO ON..... the wyld is constantly corrupting those places.<br /> <br /> But in the &quot;center of Creation&quot; is the Elemental Pole of Earth really distant from the wyld thus is OK to live there (Thank you Epic Solars Artifacts and Scaret Queen). If that is the initial argument then the opposite side of the world would be THE PUREST CHAOS/WYLD FAIR FOLK KINGS TERRITORY. (Painted in Radiactive Green for educational reference). All other crazy red texture nonsense is the Wyld. I believe half (or even more) of the world is truly engulfed by Wyld. /o\\<br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt; Enough of talking check this out &gt;&gt;&gt; Link for the updated Globe Map &gt;&gt;&gt; <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/rkmAw2ql4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.maptoglobe.com/rkmAw2ql4</a><br /> <br /> Did I get that right? Someone have suggestions for me to update the Creation Globe Map?<br /> <br /> Cya <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":{"userid":2498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","user":"Yukiartic","date":". 12-21-2018, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","name":"Yukiartic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T11:49:42-08:00","id":1276097,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I still think a globe has no real advantages over a flat world if you can't go around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T19:52:05-08:00","id":1276171,"title":"","content":"Tried adding a second map reversed, and while it helped with some things, it exacerbated some others. Maybe someone else who knows a bit more about this can do something better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/H1ePrK2lV\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/H1ePrK2lV\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.maptoglobe.com/H1ePrK2lV